  "sport": "hockey",
  "title": "Four lines – passing variations",
  "description": "Four lines standing in pairs facing each other, two on the left and two on the right. The first in a line passes and then skates on according to the variation you are playing:\n1. Pass forward and go to the back of your own line.\n2. Pass forward and follow your pass to the line you passed to.\n3. Pass sideways and switch to the line straight ahead.\n4. Pass straight ahead and switch to the line beside you.\n5. Pass diagonally and switch straight ahead or sideways.\n\nVary the passes: forehand, backhand, first time, saucer passes and off the boards. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Pass along the ice to the receiver's blade."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Receive with a soft blade and move the puck on quickly."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Skate straight after the pass so the lines never stand still."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "difficulty": 1,
